# Target C — concurrent Sections 122–123 promotion audit

**Date:** 2026-09-12  
**Verdict:** **PASS.**  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** **STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.**

Two proof-only results landed on `main` during the audit. They were both numbered 120/121, colliding with the already-audited anisotropic-return/local-Oler pair. This audit normalizes the later pair as Sections **122–123** and checks their finite proof chains against the current canonical stack.

## 1. Section 122 — aggregate two-arc detour

The theorem is valid.

Canonical Section 116 supplies, cell by cell,

\[
d_rE_r\ge(4-2\sqrt3)A_{4,r},
\qquad
E_r=L_r+P_{{\rm exc},r}-2d_r.
\]

The only possible globalization trap is double counting. The proof avoids it correctly by summing only unloaded-only rhombi. Such a rhombus has a connected four-cycle of unloaded vertices and therefore belongs to exactly one unloaded component. Hence

\[
\sum_rA_{4,r}^0=A_4^0
\]

is genuinely injective in area. No injectivity of local boundary occurrences is asserted or required.

Since `d_r<=D`,

\[
\sum_rE_r\ge {4-2\sqrt3\over D}A_4^0.
\]

In Type II, canonical Sections 80/83 give `A_4/D^2->pi/4` and only `O(D)` loaded-touching rhombi, so `A_4^0/D^2->pi/4`. Therefore

\[
\liminf {1\over D}\sum_rE_r
\ge {\pi\over2}(2-\sqrt3).
\]

No carrier selection, phase bin, KKT coefficient floor, or isolated-source deletion is used.

**Disposition:** canonical as `C-AGGREGATE-TWO-ARC-DETOUR`.

## 2. Section 123 — augmented-cell defect budget

The theorem is valid.

For one unloaded component, augment the internal/attachment contact graph by the convex attachment-polygon sides. The graph is connected, all unloaded vertices are inside the polygon, and its outer face is the simple attachment cycle. Euler plus face incidence gives exactly

\[
a_r-3-s_r={a_r-T_r+Q_r^+\over2}.
\]

The edge count is not overcounted: the starting graph contains only internal and attachment contacts, so loaded-loaded polygon-side contacts are not already present there as graph edges.

Triangulating the pairwise interior-disjoint convex attachment cells gives a noncrossing straight-line graph on the `q` loaded vertices in convex position. Thus

\[
d_{tile}=q-2-\sum_r(a_r-2)\ge0.
\]

Combining this with the canonical Section-62 pinned ledger yields

\[
e_{BB}-k
={1\over2}\sum_r(a_r-T_r+Q_r^+)+d_{tile},
\]

and consequently

\[
\sum_rQ_r^+\le2(e_{BB}-k).
\]

The comparison with the actual induced graph is also valid. Adding loaded-loaded contact chords cannot increase total `(deg-4)_+` defect because splitting a face of degree `m` into `m_1,m_2` with `m_1+m_2=m+2` satisfies

\[
(m_1-4)_++(m_2-4)_+\le(m-4)_+.
\]

Hence `Q_r<=Q_r^+`. Since every bounded nonquadrilateral face has degree at least five,

\[
P_{{\rm exc},r}=4f_r+Q_r\le5Q_r\le5Q_r^+.
\]

Summing gives the claimed global payment theorem

\[
\boxed{\sum_rP_{{\rm exc},r}\le10(e_{BB}-k).}
\]

This theorem does not assert global injectivity of local outer-walk occurrences.

**Disposition:** canonical as `C-AUGMENTED-CELL-DEFECT-BUDGET`.

## 3. Frontier effect

Together, Sections 122–123 give

\[
\liminf {1\over D}
\sum_r(L_r+P_{{\rm exc},r}-2d_r)
\ge {\pi\over2}(2-\sqrt3),
\]

while

\[
\sum_rP_{{\rm exc},r}\le10(e_{BB}-k).
\]

Thus the bounded-defect-face part of the aggregate return demand is paid by one global loaded-hull scalar. The remaining source-level quantity is the aggregate outer-walk detour `sum_r(L_r-2d_r)` coupled to `e_BB-k` and the diameter graph.

This is new structural progress but not C-II closure. The strongest explicit carrier coefficient remains canonical Section 118's `0.9762439137425688...`.

## 4. Repository validation

The audit.46 finalization run regenerated the theorem-state views and passed the native theorem-state unit tests, manifest/graph checker, active-route summary checker, and every registered theorem certificate. During that validation one pre-existing Section-115 certificate exposed a platform-sensitive decimal assertion for the transcendental tooth root: the computed root moved by about `2e-13` while the actual contradiction margin remained `3.00218e-5`. The certificate was repaired to certify the defining equation residual and retain a `5e-13` cross-platform decimal regression tolerance. No Section-115 theorem inequality or margin was weakened.

The audit.46 authority transaction is therefore mechanically consistent after this numerical-portability repair.